			<Text TI="">CDC emergency running</Text>
		</Name>
		<diskreterSW></diskreterSW>
		<analogerSWunten></analogerSWunten>
		<analogerSWoben></analogerSWoben>
		<SWE></SWE>
		<SWF></SWF>
		<Meldungstext>\T\L\S\K\ACDC emergency running A.\L\S\K\N
 System switches the solenoid valves, the relay and the height sensor off (this action
 closes the valves; no control is possible). No check for OK again! Faults remain static in the fault memory; the warning lamp is always on with terminal 15.\L\S\K\A
 CDC emergency running B.\L\S\K\N
 System switches the solenoid valves and the relay (this action closes the valves; no control is possible). After a check for OK again in the next driving cycle (terminal 15 change-over) this state is quit and the fault is set as sporadic.\L\S\K\A
 CDC emergency running C.\L\S\K\N
 System switches the solenoid valves and the relay off. After a check for OK again in the same driving cycle, the system switches back to normal operation, the warning lamp is switched off and the fault is flagged as sporadic.\L\S\K\A
 CDC emergency running D.\L\S\K\N
 The compressor and pressure accumulator are switched permanently off. It is no longer possible to adjust upward to a higher vehicle level. With the now restricted possibilities, the system attempts to set a vehicle level at the default position or lower. Level balancing (e.g. to compensate for a cargo load) is restricted to adjustment to the current vehicle level if the vehicle level is too high. After
 a check for OK again in the next driving cycle (terminal 15 change-over) this state is quit and the fault is set as sporadic. \L\S\K\A
 CDC emergency running E.\L\S\K\N
 As emergency running D, but check for OK again in same driving cycle.\L\S\K\A
 CDC emergency running F.\L\S\K\N
 Control based on 3 height sensor signals. It is no longer possible to correct a tilt\L\S\K\A
 CDC emergency running 0\L\R\K\A: No emergency running</Meldungstext>
